// onsa.toml
// [test]
// spec = ["§18.1", "§2.1", "§6.5", "§2.5"]

// The start of an item is also a doc comment and the start of an attribute (§18.1), so a `{` that
// is never closed ends at them as well. These are the forms where the line of the doc comment or
// of the attribute holds no head (the head is on the next line; a line ends an item only where
// the line is not an attribute, §2.5). A line of an attribute and the head on the same line is in
// recover_item_attr_same_line.onsa. One error in each unit; the item after is read.

